        "original_id": "3d316e11-a2b0-591d-934d-e613e431c0af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Glorious Revolution, Wincanton Skirmish\n- Laws: Church Patronage (Scotland) Act 1711\n- People: James II of England, James VII of Scotland, William III, Prince of Orange\n- Groups: English Parliamentarians, noble and other Patrons in Scotland\n- Organizations: Church of Scotland\n- Places: Scotland\n\nFacts:\n- The Glorious Revolution, also called the Revolution of 1688, overthrew King James II of England, who was also James VII of Scotland.\n- The Glorious Revolution was carried out by a union of English Parliamentarians and the Dutch stadtholder William III, Prince of Orange.\n- The Wincanton Skirmish occurred on 20 November 1688 during the Glorious Revolution.\n- The Church Patronage (Scotland) Act 1711 was intended to let noble and other Patrons in Scotland regain control over Church of Scotland parish churches.\n- The Church Patronage (Scotland) Act 1711 restored a custom that Patrons in Scotland had lost during the so-called Glorious Revolution.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
