        "original_id": "3d0f4916-d553-525e-ae2e-b00ef34b7903",
        "text": "Page: Church Patronage (Scotland) Act 1711. Sentence: Its purpose was to allow the noble and other Patrons in Scotland to gain control over the Church of Scotland parish churches again, having lost that custom in the so-called Glorious Revolution.\nPage: Glorious Revolution. Sentence: The Glorious Revolution, also called the Revolution of 1688, was the overthrow of King James II of England (James VII of Scotland) by a union of English Parliamentarians with the Dutch stadtholder William III, Prince of Orange.\nPage: Wincanton Skirmish. Sentence: The Wincanton Skirmish occurred on 20 November 1688 during the Glorious Revolution.",
